@startuml
title kdiag System Context

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

actor "Cluster operator" as Operator

node "Management server" as Management {
  component "kdiag.pyz" as Kdiag
  database "Collection directory\n(gzip, JSON, Markdown)" as Output
}

file "Ansible inventory" as Inventory
file "JSON configuration" as Config
file "Read-only kubeconfig" as Kubeconfig

cloud "Kubernetes cluster" as Cluster {
  node "Cluster nodes" as Nodes
  component "Kubernetes API" as API
  component "Stacked etcd\n(optional)" as Etcd
}

component "Prometheus\n(optional)" as Prometheus

Operator --> Kdiag : Runs snapshot, report, verify
Inventory --> Kdiag : Node names and SSH endpoints
Config --> Kdiag : Limits and collection policy
Kubeconfig --> Kdiag : Dedicated identity
Kdiag --> Nodes : SCP + SSH + sudo -n\nread-only inspection
Kdiag --> API : kubectl read-only queries
Nodes --> Etcd : Local read-only health checks
Kdiag --> Prometheus : Bounded HTTP query
Kdiag --> Output : Writes one immutable-style snapshot
Operator <-- Output : Reviews report and evidence

note bottom of Kdiag
No LLM, persistent agent,
database, or remediation
end note
@enduml
